    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Plea for Rescue 6"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "For the choir director: according to “The Lilies.” Of David."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Save me, God,",
          "for the water has risen to my neck."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have sunk in deep mud, and there is no footing;",
          "I have come into deep water,",
          "and a flood sweeps over me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am weary from my crying;",
          "my throat is parched.",
          "My eyes fail, looking for my God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Those who hate me without cause",
          "are more numerous than the hairs of my head;",
          "my deceitful enemies, who would destroy me,",
          "are powerful.",
          "Though I did not steal, I must repay."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God, you know my foolishness,",
          "and my guilty acts are not hidden from you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do not let those who put their hope in you",
          "be disgraced because of me,",
          "Lord God of Armies;",
          "do not let those who seek you",
          "be humiliated because of me,",
          "God of Israel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For I have endured insults because of you,",
          "and shame has covered my face."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have become a stranger to my brothers",
          "and a foreigner to my mother’s sons"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "because zeal for your house has consumed me,",
          "and the insults of those who insult you",
          "have fallen on me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I mourned and fasted,",
          "but it brought me insults."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I wore sackcloth as my clothing,",
          "and I was a joke to them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Those who sit at the city gate talk about me,",
          "and drunkards make up songs about me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But as for me, Lord,",
          "my prayer to you is for a time of favor.",
          "In your abundant, faithful love, God,",
          "answer me with your sure salvation."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Rescue me from the miry mud; don’t let me sink.",
          "Let me be rescued from those who hate me",
          "and from the deep water."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t let the floodwaters sweep over me",
          "or the deep swallow me up;",
          "don’t let the Pit close its mouth over me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Answer me, Lord,",
          "for your faithful love is good.",
          "In keeping with your abundant compassion,",
          "turn to me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t hide your face from your servant,",
          "for I am in distress.",
          "Answer me quickly!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Come near to me and redeem me;",
          "ransom me because of my enemies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You know the insults I endure —",
          "my shame and disgrace.",
          "You are aware of all my adversaries."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Insults have broken my heart,",
          "and I am in despair.",
          "I waited for sympathy,",
          "but there was none;",
          "for comforters, but found no one."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Instead, they gave me gall for my food,",
          "and for my thirst",
          "they gave me vinegar to drink."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let their table set before them be a snare,",
          "and let it be a trap for their allies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let their eyes grow too dim to see,",
          "and let their hips continually quake."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Pour out your rage on them,",
          "and let your burning anger overtake them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Make their fortification desolate;",
          "may no one live in their tents."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For they persecute the one you struck",
          "and talk about the pain of those you wounded."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Charge them with crime on top of crime;",
          "do not let them share in your righteousness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let them be erased from the book of life",
          "and not be recorded with the righteous."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But as for me #— #poor and in pain —",
          "let your salvation protect me, God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will praise God’s name with song",
          "and exalt him with thanksgiving."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "That will please the Lord more than an ox,",
          "more than a bull with horns and hooves."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The humble will see it and rejoice.",
          "You who seek God, take heart!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the Lord listens to the needy",
          "and does not despise",
          "his own who are prisoners."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let heaven and earth praise him,",
          "the seas and everything that moves in them,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "for God will save Zion",
          "and build up the cities of Judah.",
          "They will live there and possess it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The descendants of his servants will inherit it,",
          "and those who love his name will live in it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
